{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>To receive</b> — hearing and learning from the mouth of the instructor is the taking." "<b>To understand</b> — a verb form, and it is missing vav." "<b>Righteousness</b> — inclusive of the service of Elohim and every good deed." "<b>Justice</b> — that one judge between a man and his fellow." "<b>And equity</b> — that the one sitting in judgment speak uprightly. And some say: 'to understand, to know, to do righteousness.'"], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:20:41.587129503Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}